            "keyPoints": [
                "Denmark's largest Viking silver hoard — not the Nordic region's; Sweden's Spillings Hoard is far bigger",
                "About 18.5 kg of silver, roughly 700 objects, found in Rebild, North Jutland",
                "320 pieces weighing 6.4 kg were still inside the original clay pot; the rest lay in the surrounding soil",
                "Contents include silver ingots, arm-rings, hacksilver, 47 coins and fragments, and a small Thor's hammer",
                "Coins include Arab dirhams from the Islamic east and English coins from the 900s — evidence of long-distance Viking trade",
                "Buried in the 10th century, three times heavier than the previous Danish record, the 6.5 kg Terslev hoard",
                "The finder stayed anonymous; under Danish danefæ law precious-metal finds become state property and the finder gets a reward",
                "Being assessed by the National Museum of Denmark, with planned display at the Fyrkat Viking Museum"
